{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c52b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a85a-8231-76e1-8427-bd6f7a784205"},"sequence":240,"recorded_at":1780531400000475,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4d662671-1b40-4c4a-ba35-517ccb03377e","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"4d662671-1b40-4c4a-ba35-517ccb03377e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4d662671-1b40-4c4a-ba35-517ccb03377e"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0a85a-e634-7700-abd4-d43c419d14ec"},"task_id":"01a0a85a-e634-7700-abd4-d43c419d14ec","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0a85a-e634-7700-abd4-d43c419d14ec","chunk":"Read text file `.spec/github-login-device-flow.md`.\n1|# GitHub login — Device Flow\n2|\n3|## Goal\n4|\n5|Connect GitHub without manual PAT. Public `client_id` only in the app; no\n6|client secret, App private key, or token in binary, resources, state, or logs.\n7|\n8|## Config\n9|\n10|- Source: `Info.plist[GitHubAppClientID]` via `ios-app-manager.json →\n11|  macos.info_plist.GitHubAppClientID` (coordinator-provisioned).\n12|- Missing/empty → `GitHubAuth.Action.failed` with exact binding\n13|  `Info.plist[GitHubAppClientID] (scaffold input ios-app-manager.json →\n14|  macos.info_plist.GitHubAppClientID, coordinator-provisioned public\n15|  client_id)`. Local control unaffected.\n16|- Enterprise host uses `https://<host>/login/...` and `https://<host>/api/v3`;\n17|  requires its own App registration. Until configured, show concrete limit.\n18|\n19|## Endpoints\n20|\n21|- `POST {server}/login/device/code` `{client_id}` → `device_code`,\n22|  `user_code`, `verification_uri`, `expires_in`, `interval`.\n23|- `POST {server}/login/oauth/access_token`\n24|  `{client_id, device_code, grant_type: urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:device_code}`\n25|  polled at `interval`; `slow_down` adds 5s. HTTP 200 with `error` body is not\n26|  success: `authorization_pending` / `slow_down` / `access_denied` /\n27|  `expired_token`.\n28|- Refresh: `POST {server}/login/oauth/access_token`\n29|  `{client_id, grant_type: refresh_token, refresh_token}` — no client secret.\n30|- `GET {api}/user`, `GET {api}/user/installations`,\n31|  `GET {api}/user/installations/{id}/repositories` with\n32|  `Accept: application/vnd.github+json`, `Authorization: Bearer [REDACTED]…`.\n33|\n34|## States\n35|\n36|`disconnected → requestingCode → awaitingUser → verifyingAccount →\n37|verifyingInstallations → connected`. Terminal failures: `denied`,\n38|`codeExpired` (new code), `cancelled` (device_code destroyed, poll stopped),\n39|`network` (retry), `needsInstallation`/`needsApproval` (grant access), `sso`,\n40|`revoked`/`unauthorized` (relogin), `rateLimited` (stale + local works).\n41|\n42|## Storage\n43|\n44|- Keychain service `works.relux.runnercontrol.github-token`, account\n45|  `<serverHost>:<userID>:<clientID>`, JSON `{accessToken, refreshToken?,\n46|  expiresAt?}`. Atomic save; `deleteAll` sweeps by prefix/suffix.\n47|- Relux state holds username, IDs, hosts, timestamps only. `device_code`,\n48|  access/refresh tokens live in Flow actor privates + Keychain.\n49|- `GitHubRedaction.sanitize` scrubs exact secrets plus\n50|  `\"access_token\"/\"refresh_token\"/\"device_code\"` JSON shapes.\n51|\n52|## Refresh\n53|\n54|`GitHubTokenRefresh.refresh` is an actor: concurrent callers with the same\n55|`current` coalesce to one HTTP refresh (second caller sees the new store\n56|value and returns without network). Missing refresh token →\n57|`tokenRefreshFailed`; `invalid_grant` → `revoked`.\n58|\n59|## Guards\n60|\n61|- `PATGuard` rejects `ghp_*` / `github_pat_*` with `patNotSupported`. No PAT\n62|  UI exists; injected PATs fail closed.\n63|- `RESTMapper`: 401 → `unauthorized`; 403 inspects body for SSO/rate-limit,\n64|  else `forbidden`; 429 → `rateLimited`. Login-phase 401/revoked → relogin;\n65|  connected-phase 403/offline/rate-limit → `syncFailed` (stale, local works).\n66|- `AppConfig.auditNoSecrets` rejects plist keys containing `secret`,\n67|  `private_key`/`privatekey`, `token` (except `GitHubAppClientID`).\n68|\n69|## Session restore\n70|\n71|- `GitHubAuth.Effect.restoreSession` runs once at startup (`AppRegistry`).\n72|  It loads non-secret identity (`serverHost`, `userID`, `clientID`,\n73|  `username`) from UserDefaults, loads the Keychain record, validates via\n74|  `GET /user`, then loads installations (+ first-installation repositories).\n75|- 401/revoked/`invalid_grant` clears Keychain + identity and requires\n76|  relogin. Exception: a 401 with an unrefreshed expiring token (refresh\n77|  failed transiently) blames the expired access token, keeps storage, and\n78|  reports stale so a later tick can retry. Offline/403 keeps the restored\n79|  session with a stale `syncFailed` marker; logout stays available and\n80|  deletes both stores.\n81|- Identity holds no tokens. `logout` also clears persisted stores when the\n82|  in-memory session is already gone, so relaunch can never orphan tokens.\n83|\n84|## Lifecycle boundary\n85|\n86|- `beginLogin`/`cancelLogin`/`logout` bump the Flow `generation` and cancel\n87|  the poll plus the in-flight token refresh. `restoreSession`,\n88|  `restoreInstallations`, `refreshInstallations`, `selectInstallation`,\n89|  and `currentToken` capture the generation at entry and stop silently\n90|  after every `await` once superseded: no state emission, no\n91|  session/identity restore, no token saves.\n92|- A cancelled refresh surfaces `CancellationError` and never writes the\n93|  refreshed record (pre-save check plus compare-and-delete for a\n94|  cancel that lands mid-save). Revoked sessions surface relogin from\n95|  both refresh and select paths.","final_result":true}}}
