{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c52f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a85a-8231-76e1-8427-bd6f7a784205"},"sequence":242,"recorded_at":1780531400000479,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4d662671-1b40-4c4a-ba35-517ccb03377e","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"4d662671-1b40-4c4a-ba35-517ccb03377e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4d662671-1b40-4c4a-ba35-517ccb03377e"},"call_id":"call_01a0a85adf5872358a6fbd1e78bfb286","text":"Read text file `Packages/RunnerControlCore/Sources/RunnerDiscovery.swift`.\n1|import Foundation\n2|\n3|/// Read-only discovery of user-owned runner service manifests. Never runs scripts.\n4|public enum RunnerDiscovery {\n5|    public static func installed(home: URL = FileManager.default.homeDirectoryForCurrentUser) -> [Runners.Definition] {\n6|        let fm = FileManager.default\n7|        let launchAgents = home.appendingPathComponent(\"Library/LaunchAgents\")\n8|        let root = home.appendingPathComponent(\"Library/GitHubActions\")\n9|        let agents = (try? fm.contentsOfDirectory(at: launchAgents, includingPropertiesForKeys: nil)) ?? []\n10|        let folders = (try? fm.contentsOfDirectory(at: root, includingPropertiesForKeys: nil)) ?? []\n11|        // Prefer a standard service when both manifests describe the same registration.\n12|        let candidates = agents.filter { $0.lastPathComponent.hasPrefix(\"actions.runner.\") && $0.pathExtension == \"plist\" }.sorted { $0.path < $1.path }\n13|            + folders.sorted { $0.path < $1.path }.map { $0.appendingPathComponent(\"manual-service.plist\") }\n14|        var ids = Set<String>()\n15|        var directories = Set<String>()\n16|        return candidates.compactMap { manifest in\n17|            guard let data = try? Data(contentsOf: manifest),\n18|                  let object = try? PropertyListSerialization.propertyList(from: data, format: nil) as? [String: Any],\n19|                  let label = object[\"Label\"] as? String, label.hasPrefix(\"actions.runner.\"),\n20|                  let path = object[\"WorkingDirectory\"] as? String, path.hasPrefix(\"/\"),\n21|                  let args = object[\"ProgramArguments\"] as? [String],\n22|                  args == [URL(fileURLWithPath: path).appendingPathComponent(\"runsvc.sh\").path] else { return nil }\n23|            let directory = URL(fileURLWithPath: path)\n24|            let canonical = directory.resolvingSymlinksInPath().standardizedFileURL.path\n25|            guard !ids.contains(label), !directories.contains(canonical),\n26|                  let registration = try? Data(contentsOf: directory.appendingPathComponent(\".runner\")),\n27|                  let config = try? JSONSerialization.jsonObject(with: registration) as? [String: Any],\n28|                  let name = config[\"agentName\"] as? String, !name.isEmpty,\n29|                  let address = config[\"gitHubUrl\"] as? String,\n30|                  let url = URL(string: address), url.scheme == \"https\", url.host != nil else { return nil }\n31|            let components = url.pathComponents.filter { $0 != \"/\" }\n32|            guard components.count == 1 || components.count == 2 else { return nil }\n33|            let scope = components.joined(separator: \"/\")\n34|            let settingsPath = components.count == 1\n35|                ? \"/organizations/\\(scope)/settings/actions/runners\"\n36|                : \"/\\(scope)/settings/actions/runners\"\n37|            var settings = URLComponents(url: url, resolvingAgainstBaseURL: false)!\n38|            settings.path = settingsPath; settings.query = nil; settings.fragment = nil\n39|            guard let settingsURL = settings.url else { return nil }\n40|            ids.insert(label); directories.insert(canonical)\n41|            return .init(id: label, title: name, detail: scope, directory: directory,\n42|                         githubURL: settingsURL, servicePlist: manifest)\n43|        }\n44|    }\n45|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c531","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a85a-8231-76e1-8427-bd6f7a784205"},"sequence":243,"recorded_at":1780531400000481,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4d662671-1b40-4c4a-ba35-517ccb03377e","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"4d662671-1b40-4c4a-ba35-517ccb03377e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4d662671-1b40-4c4a-ba35-517ccb03377e"},"call_id":"call_01a0a85ae07270deba72b78a04519f78","text":"Read text file `Packages/RunnerControlCore/Sources/GitHubAuth+Models.swift`.\n1|import Foundation\n2|\n3|extension GitHubAuth {\n4|    /// Token metadata kept outside Relux state. Secret values live only in Keychain.\n5|    public struct TokenRecord: Sendable, Equatable, Codable {\n6|        public let accessToken: String\n7|        public let refreshToken: String?\n8|        public let expiresAt: Date?\n9|        public let obtainedAt: Date\n10|\n11|        public init(accessToken: String, refreshToken: String?, expiresAt: Date?, obtainedAt: Date = Date()) {\n12|            self.accessToken = accessToken\n13|            self.refreshToken = refreshToken\n14|            self.expiresAt = expiresAt\n15|            self.obtainedAt = obtainedAt\n16|        }\n17|    }\n18|\n19|    public struct Installation: Sendable, Equatable, Identifiable {\n20|        public let id: Int64\n21|        public let account: String\n22|        public let accountType: String\n23|        public init(id: Int64, account: String, accountType: String) {\n24|            self.id = id; self.account = account; self.accountType = accountType\n25|        }\n26|    }\n27|\n28|    public struct Repository: Sendable, Equatable, Identifiable {\n29|        public let id: Int64\n30|        public let fullName: String\n31|        public let isPrivate: Bool\n32|        public init(id: Int64, fullName: String, isPrivate: Bool) {\n33|            self.id = id; self.fullName = fullName; self.isPrivate = isPrivate\n34|        }\n35|    }\n36|\n37|    /// Connection phases. No tokens, device codes, or secrets are stored here.\n38|    public enum Connection: Sendable, Equatable {\n39|        case disconnected\n40|        case requestingCode\n41|        case awaitingUser(userCode: String, verificationURI: URL, expiresIn: Int, interval: Int)\n42|        case verifyingAccount\n43|        case verifyingInstallations(username: String)\n44|        case connected(username: String, serverHost: String)\n45|        case failed(message: String, retry: RetryKind)\n46|    }\n47|\n48|    public enum RetryKind: Sendable, Equatable {\n49|        case newCode\n50|        case retry\n51|        case relogin\n52|        case grantAccess\n53|        case none\n54|    }\n55|\n56|    public enum AuthError: LocalizedError, Sendable, Equatable {\n57|        case cancelled\n58|        case denied\n59|        case codeExpired\n60|        case slowDown\n61|        case authorizationPending\n62|        case network(String)\n63|        case unauthorized\n64|        case forbidden(String)\n65|        case rateLimited(retryAfter: Int?)\n66|        case needsInstallation\n67|        case needsApproval\n68|        case ssoRequired\n69|        case revoked\n70|        case missingClientID(binding: String)\n71|        case patNotSupported\n72|        case tokenRefreshFailed\n73|\n74|        public var errorDescription: String? {\n75|            switch self {\n76|            case .cancelled: \"Login cancelled.\"\n77|            case .denied: \"Access denied on GitHub. Approve Runner Control or try again.\"\n78|            case .codeExpired: \"Code expired. Get a new code.\"\n79|            case .slowDown: \"Polling too fast. Backing off.\"\n80|            case .authorizationPending: \"Waiting for confirmation on GitHub…\"\n81|            case .network(let message): message\n82|            case .unauthorized: \"Session expired or revoked (401). Sign in again.\"\n83|            case .forbidden(let message): message.isEmpty ? \"Access forbidden (403). Grant the App or approve access.\" : message\n84|            case .rateLimited: \"GitHub rate limit reached. Data may be stale; local control still works.\"\n85|            case .needsInstallation: \"GitHub App is not installed for this account. Grant access to continue.\"\n86|            case .needsApproval: \"Organization approval is required.\"\n87|            case .ssoRequired: \"SSO authorization is required for this organization.\"\n88|            case .revoked: \"Session was revoked. Sign in again.\"\n89|            case .missingClientID(let binding): \"GitHub App client_id is not provisioned. Missing binding: \\(binding).\"\n90|            case .patNotSupported: \"Personal access tokens are not supported. Use Sign in with GitHub (Device Flow).\"\n91|            case .tokenRefreshFailed: \"Token refresh failed. Sign in again.\"\n92|            }\n93|        }\n94|    }\n95|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c533","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a85a-8231-76e1-8427-bd6f7a784205"},"sequence":244,"recorded_at":1780531400000483,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4d662671-1b40-4c4a-ba35-517ccb03377e","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"4d662671-1b40-4c4a-ba35-517ccb03377e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4d662671-1b40-4c4a-ba35-517ccb03377e"},"call_id":"call_01a0a85ae19c7441ab79c84a7d1a050f","text":"Read text file `Packages/RunnerControlCore/Sources/GitHubAppConfig.swift`.\n1|import Foundation\n2|\n3|extension GitHubAuth {\n4|    /// Public GitHub App configuration. Only the public client_id lives here.\n5|    /// Client secrets and private keys are never embedded (see auditNoSecrets).\n6|    public struct AppConfig: Sendable, Equatable {\n7|        public let clientID: String\n8|        public let serverHost: String\n9|        public let deviceAuthorizationURL: URL\n10|        public let tokenURL: URL\n11|        public let apiBaseURL: URL\n12|\n13|        public init(clientID: String, serverHost: String = \"github.com\") {\n14|            self.clientID = clientID\n15|            self.serverHost = serverHost\n16|            if serverHost == \"github.com\" || serverHost == \"www.github.com\" {\n17|                self.deviceAuthorizationURL = URL(string: \"https://github.com/login/device/code\")!\n18|                self.tokenURL = URL(string: \"https://github.com/login/oauth/access_token\")!\n19|                self.apiBaseURL = URL(string: \"https://api.github.com\")!\n20|            } else {\n21|                self.deviceAuthorizationURL = URL(string: \"https://\\(serverHost)/login/device/code\")!\n22|                self.tokenURL = URL(string: \"https://\\(serverHost)/login/oauth/access_token\")!\n23|                self.apiBaseURL = URL(string: \"https://\\(serverHost)/api/v3\")!\n24|            }\n25|        }\n26|\n27|        /// Exact scaffold binding the coordinator must provision.\n28|        public static let missingBindingHelp = \"Info.plist[GitHubAppClientID] (scaffold input ios-app-manager.json → macos.info_plist.GitHubAppClientID, coordinator-provisioned public client_id)\"\n29|\n30|        public static func current(bundle: Bundle = .main, serverHost: String = \"github.com\") throws -> Self {\n31|            if let info = bundle.infoDictionary {\n32|                try auditNoSecrets(in: info)\n33|            }\n34|            let raw = bundle.object(forInfoDictionaryKey: \"GitHubAppClientID\") as? String\n35|            let trimmed = raw?.trimmingCharacters(in: .whitespacesAndNewlines) ?? \"\"\n36|            guard !trimmed.isEmpty else {\n37|                throw ConfigError.missingClientID(binding: missingBindingHelp)\n38|            }\n39|            return Self(clientID: trimmed, serverHost: serverHost)\n40|        }\n41|\n42|        /// Fail-closed audit: Info.plist must not carry secrets or private keys.\n43|        public static func auditNoSecrets(in dictionary: [String: Any]) throws {\n44|            let forbidden = [\"secret\", \"private_key\", \"privatekey\", \"token\"]\n45|            for key in dictionary.keys {\n46|                let lowered = key.lowercased()\n47|                for token in forbidden where lowered.contains(token) {\n48|                    if key == \"GitHubAppClientID\" { continue }\n49|                    throw ConfigError.embeddedSecret(key: key)\n50|                }\n51|            }\n52|        }\n53|    }\n54|\n55|    public enum ConfigError: LocalizedError, Sendable, Equatable {\n56|        case missingClientID(binding: String)\n57|        case embeddedSecret(key: String)\n58|        case unsupportedEnterprise(host: String)\n59|\n60|        public var errorDescription: String? {\n61|            switch self {\n62|            case .missingClientID(let binding):\n63|                \"GitHub App client_id is not provisioned. Missing binding: \\(binding).\"\n64|            case .embeddedSecret(let key):\n65|                \"Refusing to load embedded secret '\\(key)'. Secrets must stay in Keychain, never in plist/state/logs.\"\n66|            case .unsupportedEnterprise(let host):\n67|                \"GitHub Enterprise Server '\\(host)' needs its own App registration and Device Flow support check. Local control remains available offline.\"\n68|            }\n69|        }\n70|    }\n71|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c535","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a85a-8231-76e1-8427-bd6f7a784205"},"sequence":245,"recorded_at":1780531400000485,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4d662671-1b40-4c4a-ba35-517ccb03377e","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"4d662671-1b40-4c4a-ba35-517ccb03377e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4d662671-1b40-4c4a-ba35-517ccb03377e"},"call_id":"call_01a0a85ae28d7346a9719e5af9968798","text":"Read text file `.spec/github-login-device-flow.md`.\n1|# GitHub login — Device Flow\n2|\n3|## Goal\n4|\n5|Connect GitHub without manual PAT. Public `client_id` only in the app; no\n6|client secret, App private key, or token in binary, resources, state, or logs.\n7|\n8|## Config\n9|\n10|- Source: `Info.plist[GitHubAppClientID]` via `ios-app-manager.json →\n11|  macos.info_plist.GitHubAppClientID` (coordinator-provisioned).\n12|- Missing/empty → `GitHubAuth.Action.failed` with exact binding\n13|  `Info.plist[GitHubAppClientID] (scaffold input ios-app-manager.json →\n14|  macos.info_plist.GitHubAppClientID, coordinator-provisioned public\n15|  client_id)`. Local control unaffected.\n16|- Enterprise host uses `https://<host>/login/...` and `https://<host>/api/v3`;\n17|  requires its own App registration. Until configured, show concrete limit.\n18|\n19|## Endpoints\n20|\n21|- `POST {server}/login/device/code` `{client_id}` → `device_code`,\n22|  `user_code`, `verification_uri`, `expires_in`, `interval`.\n23|- `POST {server}/login/oauth/access_token`\n24|  `{client_id, device_code, grant_type: urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:device_code}`\n25|  polled at `interval`; `slow_down` adds 5s. HTTP 200 with `error` body is not\n26|  success: `authorization_pending` / `slow_down` / `access_denied` /\n27|  `expired_token`.\n28|- Refresh: `POST {server}/login/oauth/access_token`\n29|  `{client_id, grant_type: refresh_token, refresh_token}` — no client secret.\n30|- `GET {api}/user`, `GET {api}/user/installations`,\n31|  `GET {api}/user/installations/{id}/repositories` with\n32|  `Accept: application/vnd.github+json`, `Authorization: Bearer [REDACTED]…`.\n33|\n34|## States\n35|\n36|`disconnected → requestingCode → awaitingUser → verifyingAccount →\n37|verifyingInstallations → connected`. Terminal failures: `denied`,\n38|`codeExpired` (new code), `cancelled` (device_code destroyed, poll stopped),\n39|`network` (retry), `needsInstallation`/`needsApproval` (grant access), `sso`,\n40|`revoked`/`unauthorized` (relogin), `rateLimited` (stale + local works).\n41|\n42|## Storage\n43|\n44|- Keychain service `works.relux.runnercontrol.github-token`, account\n45|  `<serverHost>:<userID>:<clientID>`, JSON `{accessToken, refreshToken?,\n46|  expiresAt?}`. Atomic save; `deleteAll` sweeps by prefix/suffix.\n47|- Relux state holds username, IDs, hosts, timestamps only. `device_code`,\n48|  access/refresh tokens live in Flow actor privates + Keychain.\n49|- `GitHubRedaction.sanitize` scrubs exact secrets plus\n50|  `\"access_token\"/\"refresh_token\"/\"device_code\"` JSON shapes.\n51|\n52|## Refresh\n53|\n54|`GitHubTokenRefresh.refresh` is an actor: concurrent callers with the same\n55|`current` coalesce to one HTTP refresh (second caller sees the new store\n56|value and returns without network). Missing refresh token →\n57|`tokenRefreshFailed`; `invalid_grant` → `revoked`.\n58|\n59|## Guards\n60|\n61|- `PATGuard` rejects `ghp_*` / `github_pat_*` with `patNotSupported`. No PAT\n62|  UI exists; injected PATs fail closed.\n63|- `RESTMapper`: 401 → `unauthorized`; 403 inspects body for SSO/rate-limit,\n64|  else `forbidden`; 429 → `rateLimited`. Login-phase 401/revoked → relogin;\n65|  connected-phase 403/offline/rate-limit → `syncFailed` (stale, local works).\n66|- `AppConfig.auditNoSecrets` rejects plist keys containing `secret`,\n67|  `private_key`/`privatekey`, `token` (except `GitHubAppClientID`).\n68|\n69|## Session restore\n70|\n71|- `GitHubAuth.Effect.restoreSession` runs once at startup (`AppRegistry`).\n72|  It loads non-secret identity (`serverHost`, `userID`, `clientID`,\n73|  `username`) from UserDefaults, loads the Keychain record, validates via\n74|  `GET /user`, then loads installations (+ first-installation repositories).\n75|- 401/revoked/`invalid_grant` clears Keychain + identity and requires\n76|  relogin. Exception: a 401 with an unrefreshed expiring token (refresh\n77|  failed transiently) blames the expired access token, keeps storage, and\n78|  reports stale so a later tick can retry. Offline/403 keeps the restored\n79|  session with a stale `syncFailed` marker; logout stays available and\n80|  deletes both stores.\n81|- Identity holds no tokens. `logout` also clears persisted stores when the\n82|  in-memory session is already gone, so relaunch can never orphan tokens.\n83|\n84|## Lifecycle boundary\n85|\n86|- `beginLogin`/`cancelLogin`/`logout` bump the Flow `generation` and cancel\n87|  the poll plus the in-flight token refresh. `restoreSession`,\n88|  `restoreInstallations`, `refreshInstallations`, `selectInstallation`,\n89|  and `currentToken` capture the generation at entry and stop silently\n90|  after every `await` once superseded: no state emission, no\n91|  session/identity restore, no token saves.\n92|- A cancelled refresh surfaces `CancellationError` and never writes the\n93|  refreshed record (pre-save check plus compare-and-delete for a\n94|  cancel that lands mid-save). Revoked sessions surface relogin from\n95|  both refresh and select paths.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
