{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e633","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a85a-8231-76e1-8427-bd6f7a784205"},"sequence":4468,"recorded_at":1780531400008931,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4d662671-1b40-4c4a-ba35-517ccb03377e","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"4d662671-1b40-4c4a-ba35-517ccb03377e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4d662671-1b40-4c4a-ba35-517ccb03377e"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Registration wizard is handed off to review (`to-review`, 14/14 checklist, outcome artifact attached).\n\nWhat shipped, all uncommitted in the Story worktree for snapshot:\n\n- **New Relux `RunnerRegistration` module** (10 Core files): actor Flow + State/Reducer + Module, `GitHubRunnerAPIClient` (downloads, registration tokens, runners, groups, labels), `RunnerInstallerService` (download → SHA-256 verify → extract → `runsvc.sh` install → exact `config.sh` → manual LaunchAgent plist), Keychain-only short-lived token store, and pure validation gates.\n- **Wizard UI**: `RunnerRegistrationPage` + `RunnerRegistrationContainer` sheet in the management window with an \"Add runner…\" entry; org flow uses a dedicated per-Mac group with editable repo access, repo flow stays group-free; permission errors are retained, not cleared by draft edits.\n- **Tests**: 35 new committed Swift Testing tests, all driving production entry points (`Flow.apply`, installer methods, reducer, discovery). Full suite: **99/99 pass**; `xcodebuild` app build succeeds; lint on new files has **0 errors**.\n\nEvidence highlights: AC coverage **21 of 21 rows** with named call sites, and **8 narrowing mutants (M1–M8) all killed, 0 survivors** — including a token-preserving redaction mutant killed by the behavioral installer test. Integrity is pinned against the system `shasum` oracle, and wizard output is proven discoverable by production `RunnerDiscovery`.\n\nBounds: no live GitHub calls were made (endpoint shapes per REST docs; live smoke is a separate delivery task), existing production runners were untouched, and UI is build-verified only per the no-UI-tests constraint.","reason":null}}
